# A1-P02 — The Wrong Weapon. Source: Production Master 2.1, lines 1221–1311.
# Scene: scenes/chapter1/elara_meeting.tscn. The combat tutorial happens only
# when danger can't be avoided: the slime follows if you back off and attacks
# if you wait.
# Every branch keeps Elara with Kaelen. The legacy flags ch1_elara_trusted and
# ch1_elara_cautious are what GameManager.has_elara() reads.
# rhythm: clipped after_slime
# (Elara's questioning at bow-point is meant to be terse: name, origin, facts.)

~ start
Kaelen: Hang on. Why is there a sword on my belt?
Kaelen: I don't own a sword. I own a laptop bag, and I don't even know where that is.
Kaelen: Okay. Either somebody buckled it on me while I was out, or—
do slime_appears

~ after_slime
Kaelen: That wasn't blood. It didn't bleed, it just came apart, like it forgot how to be a thing.
???: Were you hoping it would bleed? Don't turn around.
do elara_enters
Elara: Hands where I can see them. Both.
Kaelen: One of them's got a sword in it. Please don't— it isn't mine. Sorry.
Elara: Then that one goes down first, stranger. Slowly.
Kaelen: Going down. Point away from you. There, it's on the ground. I'm not touching it.
do kaelen_lowers_sword
Elara: Name?
Kaelen: Kaelen.
Elara: From where?
Kaelen: Flight 707.
Elara: Is that a place?
Kaelen: It's a plane. You sit in rows, and it flies, and it isn't supposed to land like— it isn't supposed to land here.
# She looks at him the way you'd look at someone describing a dragon made of spoons.
Kaelen: Did you see anything come down today? Out of the sky, anywhere near here?
Elara: You.
Kaelen: Anyone else? Smoke, wreckage, people wandering around who look as lost as I do?
Elara: No smoke. Nobody on this road but you and that thing you just cut in half.
Elara: Were there more of you?
Kaelen: ...It was a full flight.
do elara_lowers_bow
Elara: Then we talk walking. This road eats whatever stands still on it.
? Kaelen (Internal): She's lowered the bow. How much do I tell her?
- The truth. I was on a plane, I woke up in that crater, and everyone else is just... gone. => trust
- There were people with me. Help me find them first, and I'll explain the rest. => cautious
- You first. Where is this, exactly? Then I'll tell you the part you won't believe. => deflect

~ trust
set elara_first_truth
set ch1_elara_trusted
do trust elara 10
Elara: You remember them. Their faces, I mean, not just that they were there.
Kaelen: Some. Not enough. I keep trying to go row by row, and I keep losing my place.
Elara: Then keep them. Go over them on the road if you have to. I won't listen.
Kaelen: Why does it matter if I do?
Elara: Because the people who walk out of bad places usually walk out remembering less.
=> after

~ cautious
set elara_first_cautious
set ch1_elara_cautious
Elara: You pick your words like someone crossing a bad bridge. There are worse habits out here.
Kaelen: Careful's all I've got. They're out there, and every minute I stand here they get further off.
Elara: Then we want the same thing, for now. Walls first. You can't search for anyone with a slime on your leg.
=> after

~ deflect
set elara_first_deflect
set ch1_elara_cautious
Elara: You're in Oakhaven Reach.
Kaelen: Is that a country? A county? I'll take a county.
Elara: A region. The country's a long argument; nobody agrees where it starts.
Kaelen: Bigger than that, then. What's the whole world called?
Elara: Aethelgard. It was Aethelgard yesterday, too.
Kaelen (Internal): It doesn't land on anything. Not a country I know, not a word I know, not even close to one.
=> after

~ after
set elara_met
Elara: You came out of the crater, stranger.
Kaelen: I woke up in it. Climbing out was the only idea I had.
Elara: People don't come out of the crater.
Kaelen: Well, I did. I'd love to know what that makes me. Maybe not today.
Elara: Oakhaven keeps road records: travellers, strangers, and things that fall out of places they shouldn't.
Kaelen: That happens often enough that someone writes it down?
Elara: Ask Bran. Actually, don't. He'll complain about the paperwork until it's dark.
do kaelen_reaches_for_sword
do elara_raises_bow
Kaelen: Sorry. I don't know why I keep doing that. My hand just goes there.
Elara: Walk ahead of me, where I can see you.
Kaelen: Fair enough. I'd do the same, I think.
Elara: You'd do it worse. You keep reaching for that sword like it's a pocket.
do objective Reach Oakhaven. Follow the first lead on the missing passengers.
